---
import BlogsLayout from '../../../layouts/blogslayout.astro';
---
<BlogsLayout title="Intune Security Baselines: A Practical Starting Point" description="Learn how to implement and customize Microsoft security baselines in Intune without breaking production workflows.">
  <header class="article-header">
    <h1>Intune Security Baselines: A Practical Starting Point</h1>
    <p class="dek">Enforce robust endpoint defenses out-of-the-box by leveraging Microsoft-recommended security configuration settings.</p>
    <p class="meta">By Akash Nagapure · August 2026 · 5 min read</p>
  </header>
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>Understanding Security Baselines</h2>
    <p>Security baselines provide pre-configured groups of settings that help you secure Windows devices. Starting with a baseline saves extensive manual policy creation time.</p>
    <h2>Conflict Resolution & Testing</h2>
    <p>Always pilot baselines in a test group before broad deployment. Use conflict reports to track policy overrides between custom configuration profiles and baseline parameters.</p>
  </div>
</BlogsLayout>
<style>
  .article-header h1 { color:#fff; font-size:clamp(2.5rem,7vw,5.5rem); line-height:1; max-width:12ch; margin:1rem 0; }
  .dek { font-size:1.15rem; line-height:1.7; max-width:42rem; }
  .meta { color:#38bdf8; font:.75rem 'JetBrains Mono',monospace; }
  .prose { max-width:42rem; font-size:1.05rem; line-height:1.8; margin-top:2rem; }
  .prose h2 { color:#fff; margin-top:2.5rem; }
</style>